-- Step 2, Lane "syn." / "i. q." of a passage word, NOT added:
--   جُرْم, جَرِيرَة (syn. ذَنْب, Lane pp. 413, 401) — not Qurʾānic nouns; the set already has إِجْرَام.
--   صُلْب, ضَبِير, مَحْت (syn. شَدِيد, Lane pp. 1712, 1763, 2691) — not Qurʾānic in this sense (صُلْب = backbone, 86:7).
--   رَبَاء (syn. طَوْل, Lane p.1024) — not a Qurʾānic lemma.
--   حَيَاء (… "repentance; syn. توبة", Lane p.681) — a stray Qāmūs sense; not Qurʾānic in it.
--   مَتَاب (syn. تَوْبَة, Lane p.321) — same root as تَوْب; not a near-synonym across roots.
--   عُقُوبَة i. q. نَكَال (Lane p.2103) — both sides already in NS:PUNISHMENT (row added to عِقَاب above).
-- Arabic books («بمعنى», «مثل» in al-Ṣiḥāḥ, al-Qāmūs, al-Rāghib, Maqāyīs, al-ʿAyn, al-Miṣbāḥ for the 13 passage roots):
